(4726785, 679593, 52549, '<td valign="top">I agree with Sherwin, the lighting is wonderful and the image is too.</td>', 'I agree with Sherwin, the lighting is wonderful and the image is too.', '2008-05-27 05:18:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(4726789, 679816, 52285, '<td valign="top">Wow, thanks a lot everybody for the kind words, the comments and the award nomination, they are a great encouragement for me.<br/> <br/>I must say that I am not 100% satisfied of this one, because the concept is quite ok, composition is a bit scholastic but acceptable; what I don''t like is the light and the overall quality of the picture, I wanted it more luminous, more contrasted, the subject more "present" in the picture. Next time I''ll do a better job.<br/> <br/>Windtale spotted exactly what I had in mind in doing this shot, the character Molly Million that appears in various novels written by William Gibson (Neuromancer, Mona Lisa Overdrive, Burning Chrome); she had her vision enhanced with the insertion of Zeiss-Ikon lenses in her eye sockets; the name of the company was readable in tiny letters subtly worked into the patterning around each iris. The lens I used fot this photo is actually a 50mm zeiss ikon tessar 2,8 (unfortunately the compressed version of the photo does not allow to read the name of the manufacturer on the lens, but it is there and I know it ;-) ) taken from an 1936 Contax II, that appears dismantled in the hands of the "razor girl".<br/> <br/>Really thanks a lot everybody again.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-06-17 18:32:34.</i></td>', 'Wow, thanks a lot everybody for the kind words, the comments and the award nomination, they are a great encouragement for me. I must say that I am not 100% satisfied of this one, because the concept is quite ok, composition is a bit scholastic but acceptable; what I don''t like is the light and the overall quality of the picture, I wanted it more luminous, more contrasted, the subject more "present" in the picture. Next time I''ll do a better job. Windtale spotted exactly what I had in mind in doing this shot, the character Molly Million that appears in various novels written by William Gibson (Neuromancer, Mona Lisa Overdrive, Burning Chrome); she had her vision enhanced with the insertion of Zeiss-Ikon lenses in her eye sockets; the name of the company was readable in tiny letters subtly worked into the patterning around each iris. The lens I used fot this photo is actually a 50mm zeiss ikon tessar 2,8 (unfortunately the compressed version of the photo does not allow to read the name of the manufacturer on the lens, but it is there and I know it ;-) ) taken from an 1936 Contax II, that appears dismantled in the hands of the "razor girl". Really thanks a lot everybody again.', '2008-05-27 05:30:55.000000', '2008-06-17 19:32:34.000000', 0);
