(4736124, 679891, 71550, '<td valign="top">Congrats on a very nice photo.</td>', 'Congrats on a very nice photo.', '2008-05-31 12:09:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(4736154, 679455, 3724, '<td valign="top">An exceptional &amp; among the most unique contributions to this challenge. A camera depicted as ordinary object in the environment, I would have thought there would be more of these - a reminder that <i>camera</i> is an object of different forms, shape, &amp; function, ubiquitous in modern society.  A balanced composition, carefully composed &amp; thoughtfully edited.</td>', 'An exceptional & among the most unique contributions to this challenge. A camera depicted as ordinary object in the environment, I would have thought there would be more of these - a reminder that camera is an object of different forms, shape, & function, ubiquitous in modern society.  A balanced composition, carefully composed & thoughtfully edited.', '2008-05-31 12:37:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(4736841, 678603, 811, '<td valign="top">CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUE<br/>by karmat<br/> <br/>Compositionally, I like this shot.  The different circular elements set up a nice balance and contrast.  Also, I like the tight crop in this.<br/> <br/>The lighting on this is really good.  It emphasizes the shapes and textures nicely.  Also, I like the basic bw on this.<br/> <br/>I think if focus had been a bit stronger, at any point in the photograph, the shot itself would have been more effective.  While I don''t think EVERYTHING needs to be in focus, it would help if something was clearly in focus.  It does appear that the far right of the element on the right is more in focus than the rest, but it is difficult to tell.<br/> <br/>Nice approach to the challenge, and the lighting in this (again) is really good.<br/> <br/>karmat</td>', 'CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUEby karmat Compositionally, I like this shot.  The different circular elements set up a nice balance and contrast.  Also, I like the tight crop in this. The lighting on this is really good.  It emphasizes the shapes and textures nicely.  Also, I like the basic bw on this. I think if focus had been a bit stronger, at any point in the photograph, the shot itself would have been more effective.  While I don''t think EVERYTHING needs to be in focus, it would help if something was clearly in focus.  It does appear that the far right of the element on the right is more in focus than the rest, but it is difficult to tell. Nice approach to the challenge, and the lighting in this (again) is really good. karmat', '2008-05-31 23:14:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(4736868, 678444, 88136, '<td valign="top">HI from the critique club!<br/>i remember this image, i voted on it, gave it a 7. i thought it was a lovely idea. some things i might have done differently would be to level the camera with the bottom of the photo. i also would have either taken off the strap or perhaps curled it around the front so that it did not make the photo feel unbalanced. maybe dodging the background to create a brighter white rather than the yellowish color might have helped scores. i like how the red button on the old camera and the red on the new camera look, it shows a good comparison between the old and the new.<br/>it seems stange to me that this photo did not do better, it fit the challenge well and was a great idea.</td>', 'HI from the critique club!i remember this image, i voted on it, gave it a 7. i thought it was a lovely idea. some things i might have done differently would be to level the camera with the bottom of the photo. i also would have either taken off the strap or perhaps curled it around the front so that it did not make the photo feel unbalanced. maybe dodging the background to create a brighter white rather than the yellowish color might have helped scores. i like how the red button on the old camera and the red on the new camera look, it shows a good comparison between the old and the new.it seems stange to me that this photo did not do better, it fit the challenge well and was a great idea.', '2008-05-31 23:48:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(4736875, 679871, 88136, '<td valign="top">greetings from the critique club!<br/>what a fantastic camera collection! i love the variety you show here, from the old to the new.  maybe its just my screen, but the image apears quite red, which is a bit of a distraction.  i dont like how there isn''t a central focus point.  perhaps cropping it down, or just focusing on say, the bottom shelf.  the three cameras and the statue would have been a good photo by itself.</td>', 'greetings from the critique club!what a fantastic camera collection! i love the variety you show here, from the old to the new.  maybe its just my screen, but the image apears quite red, which is a bit of a distraction.  i dont like how there isn''t a central focus point.  perhaps cropping it down, or just focusing on say, the bottom shelf.  the three cameras and the statue would have been a good photo by itself.', '2008-05-31 23:54:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(4738189, 679455, 86779, '<td valign="top">Thank you Andre, much appreciated.<br/> <br/>Funny thing is, I took a few shots from different angles to see which would work best.  Every time I moved around, the camera followed me!</td>', 'Thank you Andre, much appreciated. Funny thing is, I took a few shots from different angles to see which would work best.  Every time I moved around, the camera followed me!', '2008-06-01 10:30:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(4739027, 679749, 90495, '<td valign="top">I like to think of this ribbon as a lifetime achievement ribbon. So many of your photos deserve a ribbon, whether they were in a challenge or not, that this one is well deserved and I got to say, finally dag-nabbit! Congrats Art. :D</td>', 'I like to think of this ribbon as a lifetime achievement ribbon. So many of your photos deserve a ribbon, whether they were in a challenge or not, that this one is well deserved and I got to say, finally dag-nabbit! Congrats Art. :D', '2008-06-01 15:35:22.000000', NULL, 0),
